      "baseline_text": "<think>\nOkay, let's start by understanding what the user needs. Lucas has several requests here. First, he wants to know the address where his order was sent, the tracking number, and the current status of the order. He also wants to check the storage of a tablet he ordered. Lastly, he wants to update his default address to his daughter's in Chicago. Plus, he mentioned he's lonely and wants to chat a bit.\n\nFirst, I need to authenticate Lucas. The policy says I must find his user ID. He provided his user ID as lucas_santos_6600, so I can use that. No need to call find_user_id_by_email or by name and zip unless there's an issue, but since he gave his user ID, I can proceed.\n\nNext, he wants information about his order. To get the order details, I need the order ID. He didn't mention a specific order ID, so I should ask him for it. Without the order ID, I can't check the address, tracking number, or status. Also, checking the tablet's storage might relate to the product details, which would require the product ID or item ID. He didn't provide those either.\n\nThen, changing the default address requires modifying the user's address. The modify_user_address function needs the user ID and the new address details. Lucas mentioned his daughter's address is in Chicago, but I need the full address details (street, city, state, zip) to update it. He hasn't provided the complete address yet.\n\nHe also wants to talk for a while, so I should acknowledge that and be patient, but I need to handle his requests step by step. Let me outline the steps:\n\n1. Confirm user authentication using the provided user ID.\n2. Request the order ID to check order details (address, tracking, status).\n3. Request the product or item ID of the tablet to check storage details.\n4. Ask for the complete daughter's address to update the default address.\n5. Perform the necessary function calls once all required info is gathered.\n\nSince he hasn't provided the order ID or the tablet's product/item ID, I can't proceed with those checks yet. Also, the address change needs more details. I should prompt him for these missing pieces. Let me structure the response to ask for the order ID, the tablet's product/item ID, and the daughter's full address. That way, I can use the get_order_details, get_item_details, and modify_user_address functions appropriately after confirmation.\n</think>\n\nI'm here to help, Lucas! Let's start by checking your order details. Could you please provide the **order ID** for the items you ordered for your daughter? Also, to check the tablet's storage, could you share the **product ID or item ID** of the tablet? Lastly, for updating your default address, I'll need the **full address details** of your daughter's Chicago address (street, city, state, and ZIP code). \n\nOnce I have this information, I can look up the order status, tracking number, and product details, and help update your default address. Take your time—no need to rush! 😊",
